OL,3,AMore flights delayed after hundreds
OL,4,Acancelled by air traffic control glitch
OL,5,
OL,6,FFlight delays will continue on
OL,7,FWednesday after an air traffic control
OL,8,Fproblem in the UK has led to more than
OL,9,F2,000 flights being cancelled.
OL,11,FTens of thousands of passengers have
OL,12,Fbeen hit with disruption which saw 291
OL,13,Fflights cancelled on Wednesday after
OL,14,F1,750 were axed on Tuesday, according
OL,15,Fto aviation analytics firm Cirium.
OL,17,FNats, the air traffic control provider,
OL,18,Fblamed a technical glitch and its boss
OL,19,FMartin Rolfe apologised, saying there
OL,20,Fwould be a full investigation after
OL,21,Fadmitting resolving the issue had taken
OL,22,F"longer than hoped".
OL,23,APub: 08-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  BusinessC Nat TVF  Nat News
